1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,337
Nine forty p.m. A hit and run. The car is gone. All anyone remembers is part of the number plate.

2
00:00:08,517 --> 00:00:15,573
Two hundred cameras saw it. But ordinary cameras only record. Finding that car means days of footage.

3
00:00:16,023 --> 00:00:20,960
With OmniCamera, you type the plate once, and every camera is searched in the background.

4
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:29,157
In seconds, a red alert opens the right camera, and the car's route appears stop by stop, with time and speed, ready to export as evidence.

5
00:00:29,607 --> 00:00:41,312
And you don't replace a single camera. OmniCamera connects to what you have: IP cameras, ONVIF devices, Hikvision and Dahua recorders, even analog cameras behind a DVR.

6
00:00:41,762 --> 00:00:50,365
Every frame becomes information: a plain summary, people and vehicle counts, number plates, known faces, and the mood of the scene, from calm to critical.

7
00:00:50,545 --> 00:00:53,208
If a lens is blocked or goes dark, you are told.

8
00:00:53,658 --> 00:01:02,518
Every camera gets its own rules. Write them in plain words, draw a zone or a line, and set sensitivity, quiet hours and how often it checks.

9
00:01:02,698 --> 00:01:08,170
Alerts arrive by email, SMS or webhook, and repeats are folded, so nobody is flooded.

10
00:01:08,350 --> 00:01:16,451
Small details matter. A zero misread as the letter O is offered as a possible match, and unchanged scenes are skipped to save cost.

11
00:01:16,901 --> 00:01:23,342
For crime teams: track a wanted vehicle or face across the city, with related sightings joined into one incident.

12
00:01:23,522 --> 00:01:28,687
For government: traffic counts, crowd monitoring and a single control wall across departments.

13
00:01:28,867 --> 00:01:34,871
For offices, know who came in after hours. And at home, know when a stranger is at your gate.

14
00:01:35,321 --> 00:01:42,544
Every camera sits in a central registry and on a live map, showing its health, its department, and the areas no camera covers.

15
00:01:42,724 --> 00:01:50,449
Federation links departments without disturbing their systems. Each keeps its own video, while events flow on one shared bus.

16
00:01:50,629 --> 00:01:56,256
So a plate read by Traffic and by Police becomes one trail, and each department sees only what it may.

17
00:01:56,436 --> 00:02:02,826
Add role based access, signed evidence, regional gateways, and connectors ready for VAHAN and police records.

18
00:02:03,276 --> 00:02:08,422
OmniCamera. Your cameras already see. Now, they understand.

